 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dd4BNXEPNLB/",
 "title": "15 Visual Hooks That Stop the Scroll",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "This video lists 15 visual hook techniques designed to capture viewer attention on social media feeds. Each hook uses distinct camera movements, props, or actions to engage audiences instantly.",
 "key_points": [
  "Slide Into Frame: Entering the screen dynamically to initiate the video.",
  "Quick Zoom Out: Starting close and rapidly pulling back to reveal context.",
  "Random Object as a Mic: Holding a non-standard item like a grater as a pretend microphone.",
  "Laptop Turn: Flipping open or rotating a laptop towards the camera.",
  "Camera Pull Back: Moving the camera backward away from the speaker.",
  "Talk in Front of the Subject: Positioning the speaker directly in front of the visual location or item.",
  "Wired Earphone Mic: Holding a wired earphone near the mouth to speak.",
  "Camera Rotate: Rotating the camera angle to flip the view during the intro.",
  "Close-Up Stack Montage: Showing rapid close-up shots of food or objects stacked together.",
  "Object Metaphor: Using a visual object, like an hourglass, to represent a key idea.",
  "Split-Screen Whiteboard: Pairing video footage with a visual diagram or whiteboard drawing.",
  "Physical Timer Countdown: Placing a live physical timer on screen while speaking.",
  "Unrelated Action While Talking: Performing a task like cutting fruit while delivering speech.",
  "Driving & Talking: Recording speech from inside a car while driving or parked.",
  "Walk Towards Camera & Talk: Walking forward directly toward the lens while speaking."
 ],
 "content": "POST TEXT:\n15 Visual hooks that stop the scroll. Comment the word “Info” I’ll send you 3000+ viral hooks with Reel links.\n\nTRANSCRIPT:\nSlide into frame. Quick zoom out. Random object as a mic. Laptop turn. Camera pull back. Talk in front of the subject. Wired earphone mic. Camera rotate. Close-up stack montage. Object metaphor. Split-screen whiteboard. Physical timer countdown. Unrelated action while talking. Driving and talking. Walk towards camera and talk.\n\nTEXT ON SCREEN:\n15 Visual Hooks That Stop the Scroll (with real examples)\n1. Slide Into Frame\n2. Quick Zoom Out\n3. Random Object as a Mic\n4. Laptop Turn\n5. Camera Pull Back\n6. Talk in Front of the Subject\n7. Wired Earphone Mic\n8. Camera Rotate\n9. Close-Up Stack Montage\n10. Object Metaphor\n11. Split-Screen Whiteboard\n12. Physical Timer Countdown\n13. Unrelated Action While Talking\n14. Driving & Talking\n15. Walk Towards Camera & Talk\nFormat",
 "status": "done",
